# QGEMM decompression-coupling capture inputs

The `.ttshared.mlir` files in this directory are copies of the measured
captures in `benchmark/mlir/`:

- `q80_q80_strict.ttshared.mlir`
- `q40_q80_canonical.ttshared.mlir`
- `q4k_q8k_canonical.ttshared.mlir`
- `iq2xxs_q8k_canonical.ttshared.mlir`

They are kept inside `buddy-mlir` so that its lit tests run independently of
the workspace-root repository. Regenerate these copies when the corresponding
reference kernels or their captured IR change.

`q80_q80_kb1.ttshared.mlir` is not a copy of a `benchmark/mlir/` capture. It is
the `ttshared.mlir` stage of `benchmark/kernels/q80_q80_strict.py` compiled at
M=64, N=32, K=32, T=1 (one quantization block along K), dumped through
`TRITON_SHARED_DUMP_PATH`, and is the input of `load_chain_kb1.mlir`.
Each `*_noalias.ttshared.mlir` file is the capture of the same name with
`llvm.noalias` added to every memref argument, i.e. the IR that
`--mark-noalias-args` produces under `no_alias=True`. Load_Copy_Forwarding
forwards the load copies of a capture only with that attribute, so the tests
that expect forwarding read the `_noalias` copy; `load_chain_no_noalias.mlir`
reads the unmarked capture and expects every copy kept. Regenerate a
`_noalias` file from its unmarked capture whenever that capture changes.
